                <pb facs="0120" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg114"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Everett to Mr.
                            Legaré.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1843-06-14"><hi rendition="#italic">June 14,
                        1843</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">June 19.</hi>—In the Times of the 15th there was an
                    editorial article of considerable significance on the recent provisional cession
                    of the Sandwich Islands to the British Crown. It wore the appearance at the time
                    of being semiofficial, and from its having remained for two or three days
                    uncontradicted in any quarter I am inclined to think that it was at least
                    founded on good information. Should this be the case it may be considered as
                    certain that the Government here have made up their minds to disavow the
                    cession, and to adhere to the recognition of the independence of the
                    islands.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward Everett.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. S. Legaré</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
